[0.010, "o", "\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Why did signups fall in the week of 15 July 2026?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: low\r\nTook 88s over 5 steps, 26,607 tokens, 17 observations gathered, 15 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Signups fell in the week of 15-21 July 2026, and the decline was concentrated on mobile: mobile conversions fell 31.14% versus desktop's 16.76%, even though session traffic fell by a similar ~16.7% on both platforms.  [ga4.compare_periods fec96eaf]\r\n  The mobile onboarding-completion rate stepped down from roughly 58-62 per day to 39-41 per day starting 15 July, while desktop stayed flat, pointing to a mobile-specific cause rather than a general traffic decline.  [posthog.event_trend ab32a258]\r\n  PR #913, a mobile-only onboarding modal rework, was merged on 2026-07-14 despite a reviewer flagging that the continue bu"]
[0.000, "o", "tton was unreachable on small viewports with the keyboard open, and was shipped without the requested sticky-footer fix.  [github.pull_request_activity 86024e6c, github.commits 7303548c]\r\n  The timing (merge on 14 July, effect onset 15 July), the mobile-only scope of the change, and the specific documented usability defect together support this PR as the cause of the mobile signup decline; a pure traffic falloff was tested and does not fit because session declines were similar on both platforms while conversion declines were not.  [github.pull_request_activity 86024e6c, posthog.event_trend ab32a258, ga4.compare_periods fec96eaf]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Signups fell overall, driven disproportionately by mobile  (high)\r\n    - Desktop conversions fell 16.76% (173 to 144) week-over-week for 15-21 July vs 8-14 July.  [ga4.compare_periods fec96eaf]\r\n    - Mobile conversions fell 31.14% (411 to 283) over the same comparison, nearly double the des"]
[0.000, "o", "ktop decline.  [ga4.compare_periods fec96eaf]\r\n    - Session volume fell by a similar ~16.7% on both desktop and mobile, meaning the disproportionate mobile conversion drop is not explained by a matching drop in mobile traffic.  [ga4.compare_periods fec96eaf]\r\n  Onboarding completions on mobile stepped down starting 15 July, desktop unaffected  (high)\r\n    - PostHog's onboarding completed event shows a mobile daily count around 58-62 through 14 July, dropping to roughly 39-41 per day from 15 July onward, while desktop stayed flat around 24-26 per day across the entire period.  [posthog.event_trend ab32a258]\r\n  A mobile-only onboarding modal rework (PR #913) was merged the day before the drop began, with a known usability defect flagged and unresolved at merge  (high)\r\n    - Commit 91c3e4a, titled 'Rework mobile onboarding modal (#913)', was merged to acme/web on 2026-07-14, one day before the onboarding-completion decline began on 15 July.  [github.commits 7303548c, posthog.event_trend ab32a258]\r\n    - PR #91"]
[0.001, "o", "3's description states the change replaces the three-step onboarding modal with a single scrolling sheet and that desktop is unchanged, consistent with the mobile-only nature of the drop observed.  [github.pull_request_activity 86024e6c]\r\n    - A reviewer (sbeck) requested changes on 2026-07-13, stating the continue button sits below the fold on a 375px viewport with the keyboard open and is unreachable on an iPhone SE, and asked for a sticky footer fix before shipping.  [github.pull_request_activity 86024e6c]\r\n    - The author merged the PR anyway on 2026-07-14 without the sticky footer fix, noting it would 'follow', and the reviewer's approval comment explicitly said to 'watch mobile signups'.  [github.pull_request_activity 86024e6c]\r\n\r\nCHARTS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  onboarding completed over time\r\n  value · Mobile\r\n    value · Mobile     |█▇▇█▇█▇▁▂▁▂▂▁▁|  39 → 62\r\n                       |    ^ ^       |\r\n      ^1 Upd"]
[0.000, "o", "ate pricing page copy (#908) (2026-07-12)\r\n      ^2 Rework mobile onboarding modal (#913) (2026-07-14)\r\n      ^3 Bump tailwindcss from 4.1.2 to 4.1.3 (2026-07-14)\r\n                        2026-07-08 … 2026-07-21\r\n\r\n  onboarding completed over time\r\n  value · Desktop\r\n    value · Desktop    |▅▁▁▅▅▅▁▅▅▅██▁▁|  24 → 26\r\n                       |    ^ ^       |\r\n      ^1 Update pricing page copy (#908) (2026-07-12)\r\n      ^2 Rework mobile onboarding modal (#913) (2026-07-14)\r\n      ^3 Bump tailwindcss from 4.1.2 to 4.1.3 (2026-07-14)\r\n                        2026-07-08 … 2026-07-21\r\n\r\n\r\nHYPOTHESES TESTED\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  [supported] The mobile onboarding modal rework (PR #913, merged 2026-07-14) caused the mobile signup decline by introducing an unreachable continue button on small viewports.\r\n      The change is mobile-only by the author's own description, was merged with a known, unresolved reachability defect on"]
[0.000, "o", " small viewports, and the mobile onboarding-completion rate dropped the very next day while desktop stayed flat. Timing, mechanism (a documented UI defect blocking form submission), and platform-specificity all line up.\r\n  [inconclusive] A general falloff in top-of-funnel traffic (not the onboarding change) explains the signup decline.\r\n      Session declines were similar in magnitude on both desktop (-16.69%) and mobile (-16.68%), but conversion declines were not — mobile fell nearly twice as much. A pure traffic explanation should have produced roughly equal conversion drops on both platforms, which it did not. Ruled out by comparison of magnitudes rather than a single falsifying observation, so recorded as inconclusive rather than contradicted.\r\n  [inconclusive] A pricing page copy change (commit 77aa21b, 12 July) drove the signup decline.\r\n      This commit predates the onset of the drop by three days and affects a page, not the onboarding flow, and desktop traffic (which also sees the pricing page) did"]
[0.000, "o", " not show the same magnitude of conversion decline as mobile. Not a clean contradiction from a single observation, so marked inconclusive rather than contradicted, but the timing and platform-neutrality argue against it as the primary driver.\r\n  [inconclusive] A dependency bump (tailwindcss 4.1.2 to 4.1.3, commit a41b8c9, 14 July) broke onboarding rendering.\r\n      No direct evidence ties this dependency bump to the onboarding regression; the PR #913 review already identifies a specific, sufficient UI defect (unreachable button on small viewports) as the mechanism. Not tested directly against a contradicting observation, so left inconclusive rather than ruled out.\r\n  [inconclusive] A trial-conversion-stage effect (e.g., checkout or trial-start friction) rather than onboarding-completion is the primary driver.\r\n      The trial_started event returned zero rows for the web-app project (100001) and for the oss-client project (100002) across 8-21 July, despite the event being listed as active with a last_seen_at o"]
[0.000, "o", "f 2026-07-21T16:14:00Z. This is inconsistent and could reflect a project or filter mismatch rather than true absence; the funnel query using this event also returned empty. Because we could not retrieve any trial_started data, we cannot assess this stage and mark it inconclusive rather than ruling it out.\r\n\r\nRECOMMENDATIONS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  P1 Ship the sticky footer fix for PR #913 that was explicitly flagged and deferred at merge, prioritizing the mobile onboarding continue-button reachability issue on small viewports (e.g. iPhone SE at 375px with keyboard open).\r\n      why: The reviewer identified this exact defect before merge and it was shipped anyway; it is the most direct, named mechanism connecting the change to the mobile-specific drop in onboarding completions.\r\n      [github.pull_request_activity 86024e6c, posthog.event_trend ab32a258]\r\n  P2 Investigate why the trial_started event returns no data across both PostHog projects for the 8"]
[0.000, "o", "-21 July window despite being listed as actively firing.\r\n      why: Without this event working, the funnel stage between onboarding completion and trial start is invisible, and any additional loss occurring there would go undetected by this analysis.\r\n      [posthog.event_trend d51e618a, posthog.event_trend d896014a]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - The trial_started event is listed as live and recently active, yet every query against it (event trend and funnel, on both PostHog projects) returned zero rows. This is unexplained and means the funnel step between onboarding completion and trial start could not be verified; a hidden problem there could be a compounding or alternative cause not captured in this report.\r\n  - No Slack discussion was found either warning about the launch or reacting to the drop afterward, despite two targeted searches. This does not confirm the team was unaware, since the searches may not match the actual chann"]
[0.000, "o", "el language used; it only means we could not find a record.\r\n  - No commit activity was found in acme/product over the investigation window, and PostHog feature flag search for 'signup' returned nothing, so a server-side or flag-gated cause affecting signups cannot be fully ruled out by these tools.\r\n  - 1 claim(s) were removed because an independent check found the cited evidence did not support them. Treat the remaining conclusions with corresponding caution.\r\n  - 3 claim(s) go beyond their evidence and are retained with reduced confidence rather than removed, because the rest of each one holds. What the check found:\r\n- findings[0].claims[2]: asked as an open question, with this claim withheld, the same evidence does not establish a cause: Sessions and conversions declined across both desktop and mobile device categorie\r\n- findings[2].claims[1]: PR body confirms replacing modal and desktop unchanged, but the evidence contains no data about any observed drop or its mobile-only nature, so that connective clai"]
[0.000, "o", "m is unsupported\r\n- findings[2].claims[3]: The APPROVED review was submitted by the author (dwhitfield) himself, not the reviewer sbeck, and the 'watch mobile signups' text is a separate comment by sbeck rather than part of\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - trial_started event queries (trend and funnel) returned zero rows for both the default web-app project and the oss-client project across the full 8-21 July window, despite the event's own listing showing recent activity. This is unresolved and limits visibility into the trial-start funnel stage.\r\n  - GA4 compare_periods returned zero rows when broken down by sessionDefaultChannelGroup, but succeeded when broken down by deviceCategory; this suggests the channel dimension may not be populated for this property rather than there being no channel data at all.\r\n  - 9 of the 15 cited observation(s) returned no results (ga4.compare_periods, github.commits, posthog.event_trend, posthog.feature_flag"]
[0.000, "o", "s, posthog.funnel, slack.find_decision, slack.search_messages). Conclusions resting on them describe what was not found, which is not the same as what does not exist.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  fec96eaf  ga4.compare_periods  eval://ga4__compare_periods\r\n  7d3ee134  ga4.compare_periods  eval://ga4__compare_periods\r\n  0332a65f  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  7303548c  github.commits  eval://github__commits\r\n  86024e6c  github.pull_request_activity  eval://github__pull_request_activity\r\n  d51e618a  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  ab32a258  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  d896014a  posthog.event_trend  eval://posthog__event_trend\r\n  caf18700  posthog.feature_flags  eval://posthog__feature_flags\r\n  d9b26d5b  posthog.funnel  eval://posthog__funnel\r\n  2041f27a  posthog.list_events  eval://posthog__list_events\r\n  320352b3  posthog.list_events  eval://posthog__list_events\r\n  cb1cf0c6  slack.find_decisi"]
